# tools/al/ales_tremolo_witness.rish -- the tremolo: the triangle LFO turned on amplitude, not delay (ALES74).
#
# Season: the Six-Season double-seat, Season C thread (Lotus - the creative suite) - waymark ALES - rung ALES74.
# Design read: active-designing/date/20260814/20260814-201204_fill-ales74-lotus-tremolo-amplitude-modulation.md
# Stands on: lotus/chorus.rye (ALES71 -- the triangle-LFO driver `triangle_delay_at` this reuses, read as a gain); lotus/glide.rye (ALES70 --
# `glide_scale`, the fixed-point unit, 256 = unity gain); lotus/timeline.rye (ALES2 -- the Clip, sample_min/max, the one true saturate).
#
# lotus/tremolo.rye points the modulation family's triangle LFO at a NEW target -- the sample's own amplitude, not a delay. It invents no new
# arithmetic: it reuses ALES71's triangle_delay_at driver verbatim, reading its result as a gain in units of glide_scale, and scales each
# sample by it -- y[i] = saturate(x[i]-g(i)/glide_scale). Because every output depends only on its own input sample, the tremolo writes in
# place with NO snapshot -- the vibrato's frozen-prefix machinery falls away, making this the thinnest rung in the family. The selftest proves
# the recognition outright: a STEADY SIGNAL TRACES THE TRIANGLE GAIN, matched sample-by-sample against the driver; a hand-computed whole-anchor
# case (½ -> 1 -> ½ -> 0) matches exactly; a zero-depth tremolo is a constant-gain fader; unity passthrough is exact even at sample_min (so the
# write's saturate is a proven no-op); the tremolo voice never exceeds the dry rail (an attenuation of an in-range sample is in range); a period
# not a positive multiple of four refuses BadPeriod, a swing below silence or a negative depth BadDepth, a swing top past unity BadGain, an
# out-of-range span BadRange -- there is no BadDelay and no BadLevel, the tremolo has no delay line and no mix level. Purely local -- no delay
# line, no snapshot, no lookahead, no network, no keys, no funds, no real device, no sample rate.
#
# Run from the repository root:
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/al/ales_tremolo_witness.rish

say "ales-tremolo: Language EN — the chorus, the vibrato, and the flanger all point the triangle LFO at ONE target, the delay. The LFO driver is a GENERAL scaled triangle, though — named for its first use, it knows nothing of delay. Point it at the sample's own AMPLITUDE instead, and a steady note gently rises and falls in loudness: that is the TREMOLO, the oldest amplitude effect there is, and the modulation family's first rung on a genuinely new target."
say "ales-tremolo: Style Radiant — the law is stated positively as a recognition: the SAME TRIANGLE THAT DROVE THE DELAY DRIVES THE GAIN. The tremolo reuses ALES71's triangle_delay_at verbatim, reading its result as a gain in units of glide_scale (256 = unity), and scales each sample — y[i] = saturate(x[i]·g(i)/glide_scale). Because every output depends only on its own input sample, it writes IN PLACE WITH NO SNAPSHOT — the vibrato's frozen-prefix machinery falls away, and this is the thinnest rung in the family."
say "ales-tremolo: Lens TAME — one clip of i16 PCM, a u32 span, the scaled gain centre/depth, and a u32 period (NO num/den — the gain IS the level); the gain is held to an attenuation (0 ≤ g ≤ glide_scale), so the triangle and the multiply run in i64 and the write saturates once — a documented no-op, since an attenuation of an in-range sample is in range; a period not a positive multiple of four (or past max_clip) refuses BadPeriod, a swing below silence or a negative depth BadDepth, a swing top past unity BadGain, a span outside the samples BadRange, all before any write, the clip untouched on refusal; there is NO BadDelay and NO BadLevel; siloed to lotus/, the gain in scaled units and the period in samples, no delay line, no snapshot, no lookahead, no network, no keys, no funds, no device."

let zig = "vendor/zig-toolchain/zig"
let bin = "lotus/bin/tremolo"

let build = run ["sh" "-c" "mkdir -p lotus/bin && env RYE_ZIG=${zig} rye/bin/rye build lotus/tremolo.rye -femit-bin=${bin}"]
assert build.ok else "ales-tremolo: build failed — ${build.err}"

let outfile = "lotus/bin/tremolo.out"
let selftest = run ["sh" "-c" "${bin} selftest > ${outfile} 2>&1"]
assert selftest.ok else "ales-tremolo: selftest exited non-zero — see ${outfile}"

let shown = run ["sh" "-c" "cat ${outfile}"]
say "ales-tremolo: ${shown.out}"

let green = run ["sh" "-c" "grep -q 'GREEN ales-tremolo' ${outfile} && echo yes"]
assert (trim green.out) == "yes" else "ales-tremolo: selftest did not print the GREEN ales-tremolo line"
